by User 'admin' from IP 192.168.1.101\n2023-04-15 14:55:10, Successful login of User 'admin' from IP 192.168.1.102\n```\n\n**Analysis:**\n- **Anomalies Detected:** \n    - A failed login attempt immediately followed by a successful login from a different source IP (192.168.1.101 vs 192.168.1.102).\n- **Security Events Identified:**\n    - Unusual login behavior for the 'admin' user.\n    - Potential account compromise or brute force attack.\n\n**MITRE ATT&CK Mapping**\n- **Tactics:** \n    - Persistence\n    - Credential Access\n- **Techniques:** \n    - T1078 - Valid Accounts\n    - T1110 - Brute Force\n- **Technique IDs:** \n    - 1078\n    - 1110\n\n---\n\n### Log Chunk 2\n```\n2023-04-16 09:30:00, System event: 'Service X' started with abnormal process ID (PID) 54321\n2023-04-16 09:35:15, Warning: Suspicious file modification detected in '/var/log/sensitive'\n2023-04-16 09:40:20, Alert: Malware signature match for process 'java.exe' with hash 'abc123...'\n```\n\n**Analysis:**\n- **Anomalies Detected:** \n    - Abnormal process ID (PID) for a service.\n    - Suspicious file modification in sensitive log directory.\n    - Malware detection involving a common executable ('java.exe').\n- **Security Events Identified:**\n    - Possible unauthorized modification of system files.\n    - Indication of malware presence.\n\n**MITRE ATT&CK Mapping**\n- **Tactics:** \n    - Execution\n    - Persistence\n    - Defense Evasion\n- **Techniques:** \n    - T1053 - Scheduled Task/Job\n    - T1078 - Valid Accounts (indirect)\n    - T1027 - Obfuscated Files or Information\n- **Technique IDs:** \n    - 1053\n    - 1078\n    - 1027\n\n---\n\n### Log Chunk 3\n```\n2023-04-17 15:00:00, Network traffic anomaly detected from IP 192.168.1.103 to an external server on port 8080\n2023-04-17 15:05:25, Firewall rule modification detected: New rule allowing inbound connections on port 22\n2023-04-17 15:10:50, User 'admin' logged in from a new geographic location\n```\n\n**Analysis:**\n- **Anomalies Detected:** \n    - Unusual network traffic to an external server.\n    - Unexpected firewall rule modification.\n    - Login activity from a new geographical location by a privileged user.\n- **Security Events Identified:**\n    - Potential data exfiltration or command and control communication.\n    - Possible unauthorized change in security posture (firewall rules).\n    - Suspicious login behavior possibly indicating account compromise.\n\n**MITRE ATT&CK Mapping**\n- **Tactics:** \n    - Command and Control\n    - Defense Evasion\n    - Initial Access/Privilege Escalation\n- **Techniques:** \n    - T1043 - Commonly Used Port (port 8080)\n    - T1562 - Impair Defenses (firewall rule modification)\n    - T1078 - Valid Accounts (user 'admin')\n- **Technique IDs:** \n    - 1043\n    - 1562\n    - 1078\n\n---\n\nEach section provides a detailed analysis of the security events, highlighting potential threats and mapping them to relevant MITRE ATT&CK techniques. This structured approach aids in understanding the nature of the incidents and informs effective response strategies.", additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={'model': 'metis', 'created_at': '2026-04-23T18:53:03.424022Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 41319752600, 'load_duration': 135096400, 'prompt_eval_count': 154, 'prompt_eval_duration': 1121854700, 'eval_count': 869, 'eval_duration': 38851555500, 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'metis', 'model_provider': 'ollama'}, id='lc_run--019dbbaf-9ed6-79b3-aa55-ee7dcec6c6e1-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 154, 'output_tokens': 869, 'total_tokens': 1023})]}